  "notes": "The replay-and-interpolate school, and it is the harmonic opposite of everything else on this axis: major keys kept in the source key so the reference stays legible, complete four-chord pop progressions rather than a two-bar loop, and strings and keys *replayed* rather than sampled. That last word is the house method and it is why nothing here is `impliedByRiff` — the harmony is written out, so the chord part is the record. The drums go with it: tightest quantize on the axis at 0.9, lowest velocity variance, a clap-layered backbeat and hats \"mixed bright for radio\". The bass is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.5 because the research is explicit — \"octave leaps and 16th syncopation; movement rather than drones\". ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high: the catalog breakdowns are first-person, the drum probabilities are inference. The specific inferred parameter is `drums.hihat.rolls.freqPerBar` — the research says \"16th runs into hooks\", which is a placement, not a rate. ⚠ The fourth progression family (vi–IV–I–V) is INFERRED; the research names I–V–vi–IV, I–vi–IV–V and ii–V–I, and it carries the lowest weight. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 49 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 50 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
